An extended ROM slot the host can set: puae_kickstart_ext

The extended ROM (CD32, CDTV) was whatever the model preset named. There was no core option for
it, so the only way to point the machine at a different one was a hand-written .uae setting
kickstart_ext_rom_file - and that route does not cover every launch, because StartEmpty() boots
without a config file at all. A core option applies to all of them.

puae_kickstart_ext mirrors puae_kickstart: "auto" leaves the preset's own choice alone, anything
else is a path. Like the Kickstart it is used as it is when it is an absolute path that resolves,
and looked up under 'system' otherwise - without that check an absolute path would be joined onto
the system directory and produce nonsense.

The override is applied in retro_config_kickstart() where the preset's value is consumed, not at
the GET_VAR, so it survives the preset being rebuilt on a model change.

The option is declared with only "auto" in its value list. It is not an enumeration: the host
writes an absolute path into it directly, and the list exists so a libretro front end still shows
the option rather than hiding it.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

